#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b29adb9-e20d-5fd9-a0f3-a8db9dccdb55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $μ = 3.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095318} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfaefca-cb49-5b5b-b9e7-c3754b7e2a48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $μ = 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095319} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e96c47-f79e-536a-ad1d-9d6336897d1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ = 2$ and $μ =-2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095320} {:answer/id #uuid "eb745163-55b7-5ba8-8112-cdfc6e777bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $μ = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095321} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed03bd2-2df5-5a7a-92ac-9d5eae1675b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $μ =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ed03bd2-2df5-5a7a-92ac-9d5eae1675b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$λ =-2$ and $μ =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095322} :answer-field/id #uuid "eba78439-ab78-53b0-9a0c-a91774dec622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6df187f-d344-54eb-95de-18be02ffa7f9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-42670" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1106/Source/Images/q-42670.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $t = λr + μs$, find $λ$ and $μ$." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938412/assets/a0d9fa1c366945e5e789b6361f929357af163db2e9be4a3ccc9023c12486aca6.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=2|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-2r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-2r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-2r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$"}]}
